(d) all electrical plugs and sockets must be kept clean;
(e) microphone and headphone cords must be examined
regularly for signs of damage;
(f) objects must not be placed on telecommunication
equipment;
(g) telecommunication equipment fitted in vehicles
must not be covered in any way;
(h) handy Talkie/Walkie Talkie antennas must not be
tampered with or removed from units. These units
must be kept “on charge” when not in actual use;
(i) areas where emergency generators are installed
must be kept clean and tidy;
(j) diesel generators must not be permitted to run short
of fuel;
(k) the fuel and batteries of emergency generators must
be examined daily.
16 TRINIDAD  AND  TOBAGO  POLICE  SERVICE
S.O. No. 39 Telecommunication and Electrical System
